# - resource -------------------------------------------------------------------

<http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/phr/CodeSystem/observation-pghd-codes> a fhir:CodeSystem ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:id [ fhir:v "observation-pghd-codes"] ; # 
  fhir:language [ fhir:v "en"] ; # 
  fhir:text [
     fhir:status [ fhir:v "generated" ] ;
     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem observation-pghd-codes</b></p><a name=\"observation-pghd-codes\"> </a><a name=\"hcobservation-pghd-codes\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/phr/CodeSystem/observation-pghd-codes</code> defines the following codes in a Grouped By hierarchy:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td><b>Lvl</b></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Activity<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Activity\"> </a></td><td>Activity</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  activeEnergyBurned<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-activeEnergyBurned\"> </a></td><td>Active energy burned</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of active energy the user has burned.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleExerciseTime<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleExerciseTime\"> </a></td><td>Apple exercise time</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of time the user spent exercising.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleMoveTime<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleMoveTime\"> </a></td><td>Apple move time</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of time the user has spent performing activities that involve full-body movements during the specified day.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleStandHour<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleStandHour\"> </a></td><td>Apple stand hour</td><td>A category sample type that counts the number of hours in the day during which the user has stood and moved for at least one minute per hour.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleStandTime<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleStandTime\"> </a></td><td>Apple stand time</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of time the user has spent standing.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  basalEnergyBurned<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-basalEnergyBurned\"> </a></td><td>Basal energyBurned</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the resting energy burned by the user.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  cyclingCadence<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-cyclingCadence\"> </a></td><td>Cycling cadence</td><td>Captures the user's cycling pedaling cadence. Each record represents a series of measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  cyclingFunctionalThresholdPower<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-cyclingFunctionalThresholdPower\"> </a></td><td>Cycling functional threshold power</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the highest average power output the user can maintain for an hour.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  cyclingPower<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-cyclingPower\"> </a></td><td>Cycling power</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures power output by the user while cycling.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  cyclingSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-cyclingSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Cycling speed</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the user's speed while cycling.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distance<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distance\"> </a></td><td>Distance</td><td>Captures distance travelled by the user since the last reading.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  elevationGained<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-elevationGained\"> </a></td><td>Elevation gained</td><td>Captures the elevation gained by the user since the last reading.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  totalEnergyBurned<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-totalEnergyBurned\"> </a></td><td>Total energy burned</td><td>Captures the user's steps cadence. Each record represents a series of measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceCycling<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceCycling\"> </a></td><td>Distance cycling</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has moved by cycling.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceDownhillSnowSports<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceDownhillSnowSports\"> </a></td><td>Distance downhill snow sports</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has traveled while skiing or snowboarding.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceSwimming<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceSwimming\"> </a></td><td>Distance swimming</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has moved while swimming.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceWalkingRunning<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceWalkingRunning\"> </a></td><td>Distance walking running</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has moved by walking or running.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceWheelchair<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceWheelchair\"> </a></td><td>Distance wheelchair</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has moved using a wheelchair.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  flightsClimbed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-flightsClimbed\"> </a></td><td>Flights climbed</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number flights of stairs that the user has climbed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  lowCardioFitnessEvent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-lowCardioFitnessEvent\"> </a></td><td>Low cardio fitness event</td><td>An event that indicates the user's VO2 max values consistently fall below a particular aerobic fitness threshold.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  nikeFuel<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-nikeFuel\"> </a></td><td>NikeFuel</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of NikeFuel points the user has earned.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  physicalEffort<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-physicalEffort\"> </a></td><td>Physical effort</td><td>A quantity sample type that records an estimate of the energy the user using.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  power<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-power\"> </a></td><td>Power</td><td>Captures the power generated by the user, e.g. during rowing with a power meter. Each record represents a series of measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  pushCount<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-pushCount\"> </a></td><td>Push count</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of pushes that the user has performed while using a wheelchair.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  runningGroundContactTime<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-runningGroundContactTime\"> </a></td><td>Running ground contact time</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of time the runner's foot is in contact with the ground while running.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  runningPower<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-runningPower\"> </a></td><td>Running power</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the rate of work required for the runner to maintain their speed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  runningSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-runningSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Running speed</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the runner's speed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  runningStrideLength<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-runningStrideLength\"> </a></td><td>Running stride length</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance covered by a single step while running.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  runningVerticalOscillation<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-runningVerticalOscillation\"> </a></td><td>Running vertical oscillation</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring pelvis vertical range of motion during a single running stride.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  stepsCadence<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-stepsCadence\"> </a></td><td>Steps cadence</td><td>Captures the user's steps cadence. Each record represents a series of measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  stepCount<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-stepCount\"> </a></td><td>Step count</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of steps the user has taken.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  speed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-speed\"> </a></td><td>Speed</td><td>Captures the user's speed, e.g. during running. Each record represents a series of measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  swimmingStrokeCount<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-swimmingStrokeCount\"> </a></td><td>Swimming stroke count</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of strokes performed while swimming.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  vo2Max<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-vo2Max\"> </a></td><td>VO2 max</td><td>A quantity sample that measures the maximal oxygen consumption during exercise.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  pace<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-pace\"> </a></td><td>Pace</td><td>Pace at a specific point in time. Will be 0 if the user stops moving, otherwise the value will be in milliseconds/kilometer.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  moderateActivity<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-moderateActivity\"> </a></td><td>Moderate activity</td><td>Represents moderate (3.0-5.9 MET) activity.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  vigorousActivity<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-vigorousActivity\"> </a></td><td>Vigorous activity</td><td>Represents vigorous (6.0- MET) activity.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  moderateToVigorousActivity<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-moderateToVigorousActivity\"> </a></td><td>Moderate to vigorous activity</td><td>Weekly moderate to vigorous physical activity in minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  met<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-met\"> </a></td><td>Met</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  metByStandardRmr<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-metByStandardRmr\"> </a></td><td>Met by standard RMR</td><td>Metabolic equivalent of task (MET) calculated based on either measured, estimated or reported exercise metabolic rate and the standard resting metabolic rate (RMR).</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  crossCountrySkiingSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-crossCountrySkiingSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Cross country skiing speed</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the user's speed while cross country skiing.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceCrossCountrySkiing<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceCrossCountrySkiing\"> </a></td><td>Distance cross country skiing</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has moved while cross country skiing.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  paddleSportsSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-paddleSportsSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Paddle sports speed</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the user's speed during paddle sports.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distancePaddleSports<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distancePaddleSports\"> </a></td><td>Distance paddle sports</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has moved during paddle sports.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  rowingSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-rowingSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Rowing speed</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the user's rowing speed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceRowing<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceRowing\"> </a></td><td>Distance rowing</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the distance the user has rowed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  distanceSkatingSports<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-distanceSkatingSports\"> </a></td><td>Distance skating sports</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the distance the user has skated.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  estimatedWorkoutEffortScore<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-estimatedWorkoutEffortScore\"> </a></td><td>Estimated workout effort score</td><td>A quantity sample type that represents estimate of exertion score.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  workoutEffortScore<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-workoutEffortScore\"> </a></td><td>Workout effort score</td><td>A quantity sample type that represents exertion score.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">AlcoholConsumption<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-AlcoholConsumption\"> </a></td><td>Alcohol consumption</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  bloodAlcoholContent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-bloodAlcoholContent\"> </a></td><td>Blood alcohol content</td><td>quantity sample type that measures the user's blood alcohol content.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  numberOfAlcoholicBeverages<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-numberOfAlcoholicBeverages\"> </a></td><td>Number of alcoholic beverages</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of standard alcoholic drinks that the user has consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">BodyMeasurements<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-BodyMeasurements\"> </a></td><td>Body measurements</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleSleepingWristTemperature<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleSleepingWristTemperature\"> </a></td><td>Apple sleeping wrist temperature</td><td>A quantity sample type that records the wrist temperature during sleep.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  bodyFatPercentage<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-bodyFatPercentage\"> </a></td><td>Body fat percentage</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's body fat percentage.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  bodyMass<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-bodyMass\"> </a></td><td>Body mass</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's weight.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  bodyMassIndex<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-bodyMassIndex\"> </a></td><td>Body mass index</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's body mass index.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  height<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-height\"> </a></td><td>Height</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's height.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  hipCircumference<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-hipCircumference\"> </a></td><td>Hip circumference</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's hip circumference.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  leanBodyMass<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-leanBodyMass\"> </a></td><td>Lean body mass</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's lean body mass.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  waistCircumference<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-waistCircumference\"> </a></td><td>Waist circumference</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's waist circumference.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  boneMass<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-boneMass\"> </a></td><td>Bone mass</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's bone mass</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Diving<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Diving\"> </a></td><td>Diving</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  underwaterDepth<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-underwaterDepth\"> </a></td><td>Underwater depth</td><td>A quantity sample that records a person's depth underwater.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  waterTemperature<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-waterTemperature\"> </a></td><td>Water temperature</td><td>A quantity sample that records the water temperature.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Hearing<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Hearing\"> </a></td><td>Hearing</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  environmentalAudioExposure<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-environmentalAudioExposure\"> </a></td><td>Environmental audio exposure</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures audio exposure to sounds in the environment.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  environmentalAudioExposureEvent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-environmentalAudioExposureEvent\"> </a></td><td>Environmental audio exposure event</td><td>A category sample type that records exposure to potentially damaging sounds from the environment.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  environmentalSoundReduction<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-environmentalSoundReduction\"> </a></td><td>Environmental sound reduction</td><td>The environmental sound level reduced while user wearing AirPods Pro and using Active Noise Cancellation or Adaptive Transparency mode.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  headphoneAudioExposure<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-headphoneAudioExposure\"> </a></td><td>Headphone audio exposure</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures audio exposure from headphones.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  headphoneAudioExposureEvent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-headphoneAudioExposureEvent\"> </a></td><td>Headphone audio exposure event</td><td>A category sample type that records exposure to potentially damaging sounds from headphones.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Heart<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Heart\"> </a></td><td>Heart</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  electrocardiogram<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-electrocardiogram\"> </a></td><td>Electrocardiogram</td><td>A type that identifies samples containing electrocardiogram data.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  heartBeatSeries<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-heartBeatSeries\"> </a></td><td>Heart beat series</td><td>A series sample containing heartbeat data.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">LabAndTestResults<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-LabAndTestResults\"> </a></td><td>Lab and test results</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  bloodGlucose<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-bloodGlucose\"> </a></td><td>Blood glucose</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's blood glucose level.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  electrodermalActivity<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-electrodermalActivity\"> </a></td><td>Electrodermal activity</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures electrodermal activity.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  forcedExpiratoryVolume1<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-forcedExpiratoryVolume1\"> </a></td><td>Forced expiratory volume1</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of air that can be forcibly exhaled from the lungs during the first second of a forced exhalation.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  forcedVitalCapacity<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-forcedVitalCapacity\"> </a></td><td>Forced vital capacity</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of air that can be forcibly exhaled from the lungs after taking the deepest breath possible.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  inhalerUsage<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-inhalerUsage\"> </a></td><td>Inhaler usage</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of puffs the user takes from their inhaler.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  insulinDelivery<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-insulinDelivery\"> </a></td><td>Insulin delivery</td><td>A quantity sample that measures the amount of insulin delivered.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  numberOfTimesFallen<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-numberOfTimesFallen\"> </a></td><td>Number of times fallen</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the number of times the user fell.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  peakExpiratoryFlowRate<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-peakExpiratoryFlowRate\"> </a></td><td>Peak expiratory flow rate</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's maximum flow rate generated during a forceful exhalation.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  peripheralPerfusionIndex<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-peripheralPerfusionIndex\"> </a></td><td>Peripheral perfusion index</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's peripheral perfusion index.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  timeInDaylight<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-timeInDaylight\"> </a></td><td>Time in daylight</td><td>A quantity sample type that captures the amount of time the user spent in daylight.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  inspiratoryTime<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-inspiratoryTime\"> </a></td><td>Inspiratory time</td><td>The duration of a person's inspiration, either a single measurement, or the result of aggregating several measurements made over time.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  ventilationCycleTime<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-ventilationCycleTime\"> </a></td><td>Ventilation cycle time</td><td>Represents the duration of a person's complete respiration.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  minuteVolume<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-minuteVolume\"> </a></td><td>Minute volume</td><td>The volume of gas inhaled or exhaled from a person's lungs per minute.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  breathCarbonMonoxide<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-breathCarbonMonoxide\"> </a></td><td>Breath carbon monoxide</td><td>The amount of carbon monoxide gas present in a person's exhaled breath.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Mindfulness<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Mindfulness\"> </a></td><td>Mindfulness</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  mindfulSession<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-mindfulSession\"> </a></td><td>Mindful session</td><td>A category sample type for recording a mindful session.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Sleep<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Sleep\"> </a></td><td>Sleep</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  sleepAnalysis<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-sleepAnalysis\"> </a></td><td>Sleep analysis</td><td>A category sample type for sleep analysis information.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  sleepEpisode<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-sleepEpisode\"> </a></td><td>Sleep episode</td><td>Represents one sleep episode, which can be the main sleep event (i.e., a night sleep for most people) or a nap.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  snoreIndex<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-snoreIndex\"> </a></td><td>Snore index</td><td>The number of snore events per hour.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  snoreEvent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-snoreEvent\"> </a></td><td>Snore event</td><td>A data type that represents the loudness, duration of snoring, and the posture during snoring.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  sleepAHI<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-sleepAHI\"> </a></td><td>Sleep ahi</td><td>The number of apnea and hypopnea events recorded per hour of sleep.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  sleepArousalIndex<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-sleepArousalIndex\"> </a></td><td>Sleep arousal index</td><td>The average number of arousals per hour of sleep.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleSleepingBreathingDisturbances<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleSleepingBreathingDisturbances\"> </a></td><td>Apple sleeping breathing disturbances</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures a nightly breathing disturbances.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  sleepApneaEvent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-sleepApneaEvent\"> </a></td><td>Sleep apnea event</td><td>A category type that represents sleep apnea event.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Mobility<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Mobility\"> </a></td><td>Mobility</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleWalkingSteadiness<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleWalkingSteadiness\"> </a></td><td>Apple walking steadiness</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the steadiness of the user's gait.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  appleWalkingSteadinessEvent<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-appleWalkingSteadinessEvent\"> </a></td><td>Apple walking steadiness event</td><td>A category sample type that records an incident where the user showed a reduced score for their gait's steadiness.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  sixMinuteWalkTestDistance<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-sixMinuteWalkTestDistance\"> </a></td><td>Six minute walk test distance</td><td>A quantity sample type that stores the distance a user can walk during a six-minute walk test.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  walkingSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-walkingSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Walking speed</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the user's average speed when walking steadily over flat ground.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  walkingStepLength<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-walkingStepLength\"> </a></td><td>Walking step length</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the average length of the user's step when walking steadily over flat ground.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  walkingAsymmetryPercentage<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-walkingAsymmetryPercentage\"> </a></td><td>Walking asymmetry percentage</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the percentage of steps in which one foot moves at a different speed than the other when walking on flat ground.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  walkingDoubleSupportPercentage<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-walkingDoubleSupportPercentage\"> </a></td><td>Walking double support percentage</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the percentage of time when both of the user's feet touch the ground while walking steadily over flat ground.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  stairAscentSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-stairAscentSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Stair ascent speed</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the user's speed while climbing a flight of stairs.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  stairDescentSpeed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-stairDescentSpeed\"> </a></td><td>Stair descent speed</td><td>A quantity sample type measuring the user's speed while descending a flight of stairs.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Nutrition<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-Nutrition\"> </a></td><td>Nutrition</td><td/></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryBiotin<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryBiotin\"> </a></td><td>Biotin</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of biotin (vitamin B7) consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryCaffeine<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryCaffeine\"> </a></td><td>Caffeine</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of caffeine consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryCalcium<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryCalcium\"> </a></td><td>Calcium</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of calcium consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryCarbohydrates<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryCarbohydrates\"> </a></td><td>Carbohydrates</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of carbohydrates consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryChloride<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryChloride\"> </a></td><td>Chloride</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of chloride consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryCholesterol<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryCholesterol\"> </a></td><td>Cholesterol</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of cholesterol consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryChromium<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryChromium\"> </a></td><td>Chromium</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of chromium consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryCopper<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryCopper\"> </a></td><td>Copper</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of copper consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryEnergyConsumed<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryEnergyConsumed\"> </a></td><td>Energy consumed</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of energy consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryEnergyFromFat<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryEnergyFromFat\"> </a></td><td>Energy from fat</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of energy form fat.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFatMonounsaturated<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFatMonounsaturated\"> </a></td><td>Fat monounsaturated</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of monounsaturated fat consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFatPolyunsaturated<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFatPolyunsaturated\"> </a></td><td>Fat polyunsaturated</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of polyunsaturated fat consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFatUnsaturated<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFatUnsaturated\"> </a></td><td>Fat unsaturated</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of unsaturated fat consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryTransFat<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryTransFat\"> </a></td><td>Trans fat</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of trans fat consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFatSaturated<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFatSaturated\"> </a></td><td>Fat saturated</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of saturated fat consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFatTotal<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFatTotal\"> </a></td><td>Fat total</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the total amount of fat consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFiber<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFiber\"> </a></td><td>Fiber</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of fiber consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  dietaryFolateOrFolicAcid<a name=\"observation-pghd-codes-dietaryFolateOrFolicAcid\"> </a></td><td>Folate or folic acid</td><td>A quantity sample type that measures the amount of folate (folic acid) consumed.</td></